<h2 id=3D"Supportenable/disabledefaultstorageclass-TanzuCLI">&nbsp;Tanzu CL=  
I</h2>
<p>Already supported, by this <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://do=  
cs.vmware.com/en/VMware-Tanzu-Kubernetes-Grid/2.1/tkg-deploy-mc/mgmt-deploy=
-config-ref.html#common-variables-for-all-target-platforms-0">variable <spa=  
n style=3D"color: rgb(29,28,29);">ENABLE_DEFAULT_STORAGE_CLASS</span></a><s=  
pan style=3D"color: rgb(29,28,29);">: true/false</span></p>
<h1 id=3D"Supportenable/disabledefaultstorageclass-Supportmatrix">Support m=  
atrix</h1>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
<colgroup class=3D"">
<col class=3D"">
<col class=3D"">
</colgroup>
<tbody class=3D"">
<tr class=3D"">
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">TKGm</th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">Support</th>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"">
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">TBD</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd"><br></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Note:</p>
<p>From Xiaoshuang</p>
<ol>
<li>All TKGm classy clusters are supported, by customizing <em>ClusterBoots=  
trap</em></li>
<li>v2.3+ versions, default sc costomization is supported (by Tanzu CLI by =  
workaround)</li>
</ol>
<p><br></p>
<h1 id=3D"Supportenable/disabledefaultstorageclass-Openquestions:">Open que=  
stions:</h1>
<p>The following question/behavior is based on personal testing, appreciate=
 confirm from TKGm side.</p>
<ol>
<li>Strictly speaking<em> storagePolicyID(VSPHERE_STORAGE_POLICY_ID ) </em>=  
exposed on TMC UI, is a name i.e <em><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);">=
"Management Storage Policy - Regular".</span></em>
<ul>
<li><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);">Is this a spell-mistake or bug?      &n=  
bsp; &nbsp; </span></li>
<li><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,255=
);"><strong>Answers</strong>: <span style=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);">this is=
 a history issue, does not impact normal functionality.</span></span></span=
></li>
</ul></li>
<li><strong>Vcenter-datastore</strong> has nothing to do with <em>storagePo=  
licyID </em>for default<em> storage class.</em>
<ul>
<li>So TMC will not validate the compatibility of <strong>vcenter-datastore=
</strong> and <em>storagePolicy.</em></li>
<li><em><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0=
,255);"><strong>Answers</strong>: <span style=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);">yes=
, but <strong>Vcenter-datastore</strong></span></span></span></em><span sty=  
le=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,255);"><span sty=  
le=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);"> has to be compatible with <em>storagePolicyID=
</em> for vcenter. The <span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"><span style=3D=
"color: rgb(0,0,255);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);"><em>storagePol=  
icyID</em> is the same variable used not only<span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51=
,102);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,255);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(51,5=  
1,51);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0=
,255);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);">&nbsp;storageclass.</span></s=  
pan></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li>There may have pvc creating failure, even <em>storagePolicy </em>has co=  
mpatible datastores. <span style=3D"color: rgb(255,204,153);">Need to confi=  
rm the behavior.</span>&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 80.0px;">For example:&nbsp;</p>
<ol>
<li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
<ol>
<li style=3D"list-style-type: none;">
<ol>
<li>Set <em>infraProvider: "vsphere", </em>and <em>VSPHERE_STORAGE_POLICY_I=  
D: "<span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);">VM Encryption Policy</span>"</em>=
, hit error:<em>&nbsp;<span style=3D"color: rgb(255,255,153);"><span style=
=3D"color: rgb(204,153,255);">CnsFault error: VSLM task failed</span></span=
></em><span style=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);">, when Creating a pvc. &nbsp;<e=  
m><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,255);=
"><strong>Answers</strong>: </span></span></em>the root cause is because of=
 the <em><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);">Encryption.</span></em></spa=  
n></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">This may impact the UX experience, for ex=  
ample inputs validations.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;">So TMC will not validate the compatibilit=  
y of datastore and <em>storagePolicy.</em></p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 40.0px;"><em><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,51,102);"=
><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,0,255);"><strong>Answers</strong>: </span></sp=  
an></em><span style=3D"color: rgb(51,51,51);">need to validate the compatib=  
ility of datastore and storagePolicy.</span></p>
<h1 id=3D"Supportenable/disabledefaultstorageclass-Appendix">Appendix</h1>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong><span style=3D"color: rgb(23,43,77);">Glossary and explanations =  
from <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://docs.vmware.com/en/VMware-T=  
anzu-Kubernetes-Grid/2.3/tkg-deploy-mc/config-ref.html#vsphere-11">TKGm doc=
</a>.</span></strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
<colgroup class=3D"">
<col class=3D"">
<col class=3D"">
<col class=3D"">
<col class=3D"">
</colgroup>
<tbody class=3D"">
<tr class=3D"">
<th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh"><br></th>
</tr>
<tr class=3D"">
<td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);"><code>VSPHE=  
RE_DATACENTER</code></span></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd"><span style=3D"color: rgb(0,128,0);">govc <a cla=  
ss=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://datacenter.info">datacenter.info</a></s=  
pan></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong style=3D"text-align: left;">Required</st=  
rong><span style=3D"color: rgb(86,86,86);">. The name of the datacenter in =  
which to deploy the cluster, as it appears in the vSphere inventory. For ex=  
